<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adelaide, Countess of Vermandois</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1065–c. 1120</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adelaide">Adelaide</a> was Countess of Vermandois and Valois, heiress of the Herbertian counts of Vermandois, a branch of the Carolingian dynasty. Around 1080 she married Hugh, brother of King Philip I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, who became count through her and later led a contingent in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-crusade">First Crusade</a>. Their descendants held Vermandois until the late 12th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/adelaide-countess-of-vermandois.jpg" alt="Adelaide, Countess of Vermandois" width="178" height="442" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Abel Hugo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Adelaide_of_Vermandois.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
